  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-251017",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $m$ from $2$ to $5.$ So, computing the terms for $m=2,3,4,5$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{m=2}^{5}\\frac{2m+1}{10} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1}{10}+\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1}{10}+\\frac{2\\cdot 4+1}{10}+\\frac{2\\cdot 5+1}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{7}{10}+\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{11}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+7+9+11}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 16}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
